[i]Version 3.3.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v.3.3.4 🐛MASSIVE BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[i]This hotfix addresses many issues reported![/i]
[*]🐛 [b]Warbond Purchase Server Crash:[/b] Fixed a fatal `attempt to call global 'Server' (a nil value)` error triggered when a player interacted with the "Purchase Warbonds" option at a Trading Post.
[*]🐛 [b]Warbond Dialog Flow Rearchitected:[/b] The underlying architectural issue was that a UI interaction callback which always executes on the client — was directly calling a script to determine which dialog to show. Any bridge function that transitively calls [i]Server()[/i] will crash in this context. Reworked the flow to use the correct Avorion client/server RPC pattern.
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Failing on First Kill:[/b] Fixed an issue where destroying the very first enemy target under a new War Bounty License would fail to pay out and incorrectly tell you that you already had a License active, even when you didn't. Bounty rewards are now credited immediately when the License activates, so your first kill always counts.
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Failing on EVERY Kill After the First:[/b] Building on the fix above, every kill after your first one under an active License was also being wrongly rejected with the "License already active" message. Bounty kills now correctly register for the full duration of your License.
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty License Crash / Recurring Error Log:[/b] Fixed a bug causing a repeating server error roughly every 5 minutes while a War Bounty License was active, along with the periodic "time remaining" and "target destroyed" chat messages not displaying correctly.
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Crash on Invalid Killer:[/b] Fixed a rare server crash that could occur when a bounty target was destroyed under specific ownership conditions.
[*]🐛 [b]Blank / Unclickable Bulletin Board Missions:[/b] Fixed a major bug where War Contract missions posted on faction bulletin boards would show up as empty bars with no description and could not be accepted. This affected every faction's bulletin board and was the cause of recent reports of "blank missions."
[*]🐛 [b]Physical Sieges Not Triggering:[/b] Fixed a critical bug preventing the physical siege event (enemy Troop Transports warping in to board and capture a contested station) from ever starting. This is a core part of the Dynamic Territory Sieges feature and was completely broken until this fix.
[*]🐛 [b]Troop Transports Boarding the Wrong Station:[/b] Fixed an issue where, in sectors with multiple hostile stations, an invading Troop Transport could target the wrong station instead of the one actually under siege.
[*]🐛 [b]Shield Jammer Chance Corrected:[/b] The Electronic Warfare "Shield Jammer" effect during a siege was only triggering about 10% of the time instead of the intended 35%.
[*]🐛 [b]Troop Transport Boarding Explosion Not Displaying:[/b] Fixed the self-destruct explosion effect not appearing for other players when a Troop Transport successfully boards a station.
[*]🐛 [b]Subspace Containment Contract Could Never Finish:[/b] Fixed a bug preventing this War Contract from ever completing or paying out after destroying its target, plus a rare issue where leaving and re-entering the sector could spawn duplicate targets.
[*]🐛 [b]Decapitation Strike & Frontline Siege Difficulty Scaling:[/b] Fixed a bug preventing the intended boss/base difficulty scaling from applying in these two War Contracts.
[*]🐛 [b]Several War Contracts Could Fail to Load on Linux Servers:[/b] Fixed a file-name capitalization issue in 7 War Contract missions that would only cause problems on Linux-hosted dedicated servers.
[*]🐛 [b]Interception & Supply Line Raid Could Show "Failed" After Succeeding:[/b] Fixed a timing bug where completing these contracts at the exact moment their timer ran out could show a failure message even though you'd already won.
[*]🐛 [b]Breakthrough & High-Value Defection Spawning Extra Enemies After Completion:[/b] Fixed a bug where extra enemy waves could spawn into the sector right after these missions had already ended.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Vanguard Event Broken:[/b] Fixed this dynamic event so its boss ship and cinematic banner actually work.
[*]🐛 [b]Headhunters Ambush Never Triggering:[/b] Fixed a bug that silently prevented this ambush event from ever firing.
[*]🐛 [b]Military Outpost "Enlist" Option Not Appearing During War:[/b] Fixed a bug preventing the mercenary enlistment dialog from showing up at Military Outposts even when their faction was actively at war.
[*]🐛 [b]Mercenary Contract Kills Not Tracked:[/b] Fixed a bug preventing kills from counting toward active Mercenary Contracts.
[*]🐛 [b]Rift Hazard Sound Effect Crash:[/b] Fixed a potential crash tied to the ambient thunder sound effect in Rift-affected sectors.
[*]🐛 [b]Galactic Politics Tab Filter (Non-English Clients):[/b] Fixed the conflict filter dropdown not working correctly for players using a non-English game language.
[*]🐛 [b]Miniature/Undersized Ships in Several Dynamic Events:[/b] Fixed a sizing bug causing some enemy ships spawned by Blockade, Stranded Flagship, and other dynamic events to come out far smaller than intended.
[*]🐛 [b]Rare Crashes in Capital Ship Duel, Orbital Bombardment, Diplomatic Sabotage, and Station Siege Events:[/b] Fixed a handful of edge-case crashes that could occur when these events triggered in unclaimed space.
[*]🐛 [b]Enemy Ships Spawning Over 100km Away During Sieges:[/b] Fixed a bug causing invasion fleets to occasionally spawn nearly twice as far from the action as intended during sector sieges.

[i]Version 3.3.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.3 🐛 BOUNTY SYSTEM CRASH FIX 🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a severe server-side crash related to the new Bounty system tracking.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Server Crash:[/b] Fixed a severe runtime error that would instantly crash the sector simulation thread when a player destroyed a valid War Bounty target. The script was failing to properly identify the player or alliance before attempting to attach the tracking script and payout. Bounties will now properly reward you without bringing down the sector!
[*]🐛 [b]Dynamic War Event Crashes:[/b] Fixed several hidden crashes across multiple dynamic event scripts (`cw_armsdeal`, `cw_blockade`, `cw_strandedflagship`, `cw_distress_beacon_trap`, `cw_diplomaticsabotage`, `cw_refugeeconvoy`) where missing dependencies or destroyed faction objects would cause the entire sector simulation thread to fatally crash when the events attempted to spawn!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.3.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.2 🐛MISSION LOGIC HOTFIX🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix corrects mission completion soft-locks and navigation issues in specific war contracts based on player feedback![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Frontline Siege Contract:[/b] Fixed a bug where the mission would soft-lock and fail to complete if the target Forward Operating Base (FOB) was boarded/captured rather than explicitly destroyed, or if wreckage data lingered in the engine.
[*]🐛 [b]Sensor Deployment Contract:[/b] Added a physical HUD navigation beacon at the center of the sector (0, 0, 0) so players know exactly where to deploy the stealth buoy, resolving confusion caused by the lack of a coordinate grid.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.3.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.1 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a critical server crash related to the new Bounty system.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Sector Crash:[/b] Fixed a critical server crash triggered by an invalid sector object property when a player enters a sector where an active bounty is placed on the controlling faction.
[*]🐛 [b]Sensor Deployment Contract:[/b] Fixed a script error in the Sensor Deployment war contract that prevented the mission from correctly validating the player's distance when deploying the stealth buoy.
[*]🐛 [b]Background Script Architecture:[/b] Corrected namespace declarations across multiple background simulation scripts (Diplomacy, Expansion) that were previously preventing them from executing properly.
[*]🐛 [b]Script Optimization:[/b] Cleaned up dead code and unused variables in faction generation scripts to streamline processing.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.3.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.3.0 🚀WAR CONTRACTS EXPANSION!🚀[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ EXPANSION PATCH[/b]
[i]This minor expansion update introduces new War Contracts and the overhaul of the bounty system.[/i]

[b]🚀 NEW MISSIONS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚔️ [b]Sector Raid:[/b] Wipe out key hostile infrastructure or civilian vessels deep in enemy territory.
[*]⚔️ [b]Hunter Killer:[/b] Hunt down a specialized enemy fleet causing problems for the allied faction.
[*]⚔️ [b]Resource Heist:[/b] Infiltrate a hostile sector and forcefully harvest a massive amount of valuable resources.
[*]⚔️ [b]Distraction Carnage:[/b] Draw massive enemy fleets to your location and survive a grueling 5-minute ambush.
[*]⚔️ [b]Black Box Retrieval:[/b] Locate the wreckage of a destroyed prototype flagship deep in enemy space and extract its black box data before salvage crews strip it.
[*]⚔️ [b]Blockade Runner:[/b] Break through a heavily fortified blockade to deliver emergency supplies to a covert listening post.
[*]⚔️ [b]Champion Duel:[/b] Answer the call of an arrogant enemy commander and face off against a massively scaled Champion in a 1-on-1 duel.
[*]⚔️ [b]Sensor Deployment:[/b] Sneak into the dead center of 3 distinct hostile sectors to deploy stealth sensor buoys.
[/list]

[b]💰 WAR BOUNTY OVERHAUL[/b]
[list]
[*]⚔️ [b]Bounty Licenses:[/b] The passive global war bounty system has been entirely overhauled into an interactive "Bounty License" mechanic.
[*]⚔️ [b]Per-Kill Payouts:[/b] After securing your first kill against a faction with a global bounty, you will receive a 45-minute active Bounty License tracker.
[*]⚔️ [b]Hunting Quotas:[/b] You can now hunt and destroy up to 15 military targets under a single license. The license explicitly warns you every 5 minutes before expiration.
[*]⚔️ [b]Dynamic Reward Scaling:[/b] The base credit reward scales strictly by distance from the core. Destroying standard military ships pays out the base reward, Dreadnoughts and Bosses pay out 5x, and Stations pay out 10x!
[*]⚔️ [b]Civilian Immunity:[/b] You can no longer farm bounties by destroying defenseless mining, trading, or civil transport ships. Only military and infrastructure targets yield payouts.
[*]⚔️ [b]Galactic Politics UI:[/b] The [!] tag has been replaced with [BOUNTY]. Hover tooltips now accurately display the "Per-Kill" value rather than a flat lump-sum.
[*]⚔️ [b]HUD Alerts:[/b] Jumping into an enemy sector that currently has an active global bounty will instantly push a text alert to your HUD, notifying you that the sector is an active warzone with high payouts.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Small Tweaks & Fixes:[/b] Various small bugfixes and tweaks across various War Contracts to ensure multiplayer and alliance compatibility.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.2.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.2.0 🛠️ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ CORE ARCHITECTURE PATCH[/b]
[i]This update implements Progressive Materialization to eliminate massive lag spikes![/i]

[b]🛠️ ARCHITECTURE & OPTIMIZATION[/b]
[list]
[*]⚡ [b]Progressive Materialization (Lag Fix):[/b] Completely overhauled the [i]cw_siege_injector_persistent[/i] API. When background sieges are mathematically won by a faction, they no longer force the server to physically load the sector into memory to flip the station ownership (which caused massive server stutters).
[*]⚡ [b]Lazy Loading API:[/b] Siege victories are now queued mathematically. When a player jumps into the conquered sector, the game seamlessly intercepts the loading screen and instantly hands the sector over to the victor. Zero stutter!
[/list]

[b]🚀 MISSION ENHANCEMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚔️ [b]Deploy Minefield Threat Feedback:[/b] Improved the "Deploy Minefield" War Contract when jumping into an empty target sector. The mission now immediately spawns a hostile interceptor wave and provides explicit on-screen timer instructions (250s) to keep players engaged while the minefield deploys.
[*]✨ [b]Bulletin Board Polish:[/b] Fixed an ugly formatting issue across all War Contracts where the bulletin board would display unresolved `(${location.x}:${location.y})` variables instead of generic flavor text before the mission was accepted.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.1.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a critical logic flaw where Subspace Tears would permanently exist![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Infinite Subspace Tear:[/b] Fixed an oversight where the experimental Subspace Tear (Rift Hazard) generated during a War Crime event lacked a termination condition. It would permanently drain shields in the sector until manually deleted. The hazard now correctly dissipates once the primary target structure is destroyed and the anomaly is contained!
[*]🐛 [b]Hazard Target Detection:[/b] Fixed a logic oversight in `cw_rift_hazard.lua` where the hazard only scanned for Entities typed as Stations. It will now properly detect and deal damage to "Protection Platforms" (typed as Ships).
[/list]

[i]Version 3.1.1[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.1.1 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets a critical server crash during the Convoi Distress Signal event![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Convoi Distress Signal API Error:[/b] Fixed a critical server crash in `convoidistresssignal.lua` where `getMissionLocation()` was improperly called on the server environment. It has been safely bypassed by reading the global target coordinates, restoring the distress call event back to full functionality.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.1.0[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.1.0 ✨FEATURE UPDATE!✨[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ MINOR EXPANSION PATCH[/b]
[i]Minor Features expansion![/i]

[b]✨FEATURES[/b]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Distress Call Escalation:[/b] If you ignore an NPC distress call for too long, there is a chance the attackers will establish a permanent Pirate Forward Operating Base (FOB) in that sector, turning it into a hazard zone!
[*]🔥 [b]Bounty Hunter Ambush:[/b] If you gain terrible reputation with a military faction during wartime, they might dispatch a small elite bounty hunter squad to ambush you directly in hyperspace upon entering a new sector!
[*]🔥 [b]Refugee Convoy Gratefulness:[/b] Successfully escorting a refugee convoy to safety now grants a 1-hour minor buff called "Hero of the People", granting +10% trade prices at that faction's stations.
[*]🔥 [b]Galactic Politics Sabotage:[/b] [i]Cosmic Overhaul Synergy[/i]. You can now pay a 5,000,000 Credits bribe to the Smuggler's Market to intentionally lower the relationship between two random NPC factions, sparking proxy wars!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.12[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.12 🐛BUGFIX UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This hotfix targets an internal API math error![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Fire Rate API Error:[/b] Fixed a core mathematical error across multiple missions (Eclipse Vanguard, Decapitation Strike, Frontline Siege) where extreme `FireRate` multipliers were being accidentally applied as flat additive numbers instead of percentages, preventing those bosses from properly scaling their weapon attack speeds.
[*]🐛 [b]Volatile Shield API Error:[/b] Discovered and fixed a critical bug in Eclipse Vanguard, Refugee Convoy, and Siege events where boss shields were scaled using volatile direct-property manipulation, causing their shields to instantly disappear upon taking hull damage. They now correctly use the persistent modifier API.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.11[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.11 🐛BUGFIX & BALANCE PATCH UPDATE!⚖️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch cleans up a cosmetic bug and improves the Galactic Politics UI for multiplayer servers! It also introduces a massive balance pass to Mercenary Payouts to bring them in line with the vanilla economy, introducing Captain-Scaling mechanics similar to Cosmic Overhaul![/i]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Mercenary Payout Nerf:[/b] Heavily reduced the base payout for destroying ships (from 25k to 10k) and stations (from 250k to 100k) while enlisted as a mercenary to prevent game-breaking wealth generation at the galactic core.
[*]⚖️ [b]Hybrid Captain Scaling (Synergy!):[/b] Enlisted ship payouts now scale dynamically based on the commanding Captain's Tier and Level! Elite captains will yield massively increased payouts!
[*]⚖️ [b]Mercantile Trait Nerf:[/b] Reduced the payout multiplier of Mercantile factions from 3x (300%) down to 1.5x (150%).
[*]⚖️ [b]High-Profile Bounty Nerf:[/b] Reduced the completion multiplier for confirming high-profile bounties on Stations (from 5x to 3x) and Bosses/Battleships (from 3x to 2x).
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Multiplayer UI Bloat Reduction:[/b] The Galactic Politics conflict tracker will no longer display single-player factions. It now only exclusively tracks NPC Factions and Player Alliances.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Alliance Cosmetic Bug:[/b] Fixed a minor logic flaw where Player Alliances were incorrectly labeled as "Player Factions" in the diplomacy tooltips.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.10[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.10 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This update is a follow-up to the v3.0.9 release, catching additional background and entity scripts that I accidentally missed during my audit for fixes![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Major Event Routing Bug:[/b] Previously, several background systems (like diplomacy, news, and sieges) were incorrectly defining standard engine callbacks which caused catastrophic event routing failures under the hood.
[*]🐛 [b]Namespace Optimization:[/b] Re-aligned internal callbacks to be properly encapsulated inside their modules, ensuring proper file overwrites!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.9[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.9 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a widespread bug that was preventing almost all War Contract missions from completing successfully, alongside fixing several massive event routing bugs![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]War Contracts Soft-Lock:[/b] Fixed a massive oversight affecting almost all War Contract missions where destroyed target ships were still being counted as "alive" because the game engine preserved their tracking tags on the resulting wreckages! The tracking scripts now explicitly verify if the entities are living Ships or Stations before counting them, allowing missions to finally complete successfully!
[*]🐛 [b]Critical Event Bug:[/b] Fixed an engine-level routing issue where 5 massive events (Fleet Clash, Arms Deal, Diplomatic Sabotage, Refugee Convoy, Stranded Flagship) would silently fail to spawn their ships after dropping into the sector. The engine callbacks have been securely bound and all events are now fully operational!
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Vanguard Event:[/b] Fixed a multiplayer desync bug where the alert for the Eclipse Vanguard's arrival would sometimes fail to appear for players in the sector!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.8[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.8 🐛BUGFIX & BALANCE PATCH UPDATE!⚖️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a devastating bug with Electronic Warfare and tweaks its balance to be much fairer to defenders![/i]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ Reduced the chance for invading forces to deploy a Shield Jammer during a Siege from 35% down to 10%.
[*]⚖️ Reduced the chance for invading forces to deploy a Shield Jammer during a Fleet Clash from 50% down to 15%.
[*]⚖️ Nerfed the active duration of the Shield Jammer from 20 seconds down to 10 seconds.
[/list]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 Fixed a critical engine-level routing bug in the Shield Jammer script. The jammer will now correctly terminate itself after 10 seconds, allowing player and AI shields to finally regenerate normally. Previously, a namespace error caused the jammer to permanently lock shields to 0 forever.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.7[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]v3.0.7 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch fixes a critical crash on Linux based systems and issues with bounty payouts![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 Fixed a fatal "module not found" crash on Linux Dedicated Servers when generating siege events and wreckage fields.
[*]🐛 Fixed a missed error in a previous patch with bounty payouts!
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.6[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V3.0.6 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE!🐛[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This small patch fixes a script crash related to bounty payouts for destroying boss entities.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Bounty Payout Crash:[/b] Fixed a critical server crash in `cw_bountypayouts.lua` when attempting to award bounties for destroying boss entities. The script incorrectly referenced an `isBoss` property on the entity object directly instead of using the API-compliant `entity:getValue("is_boss")` method.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.5[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V3.0.5 🐛BUGFIX PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a script-breaking error during the Refugee Convoy event where the mod improperly modified an internal API property.[/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]API Property Integrity:[/b] Fixed a script-breaking error during the Refugee Convoy (`cw_refugeeconvoy.lua`) and Siege (`siegeevent.lua`) events where scripts were improperly assigning a read-only `maxDurability` property and a non-existent `shieldMaximum` property on ships, causing fatal exceptions. Hull scaling has been corrected to use the officially supported `maxDurabilityFactor` API under the `Durability` component, and shield scaling correctly utilizes `shieldMaxDurability`.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.4[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V3.0.4 🐛BUGFIX & ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX & GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes a critical log spam issue during Dreadnought Boss attacks as well as adjustments done to the cinematic battlefield HUD![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Dreadnought Boss Target Errors:[/b] Fixed a critical server log spam and stutter issue where the Dreadnought Boss (`dreadnoughtboss.lua`) was attempting to check the AI property `isAttacking` instead of the correct native API `isAttackingSomething`. This resulted in the boss repeatedly failing to evaluate targets properly during an attack and throwing errors twice per second.
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Battlefield HUD Sync:[/b] The Cinematic Battlefield HUD now accurately reads absolute `startTime` data provided by the newly updated Cosmic Vault API. This guarantees flawlessly synchronized visual siege progression for players who jump into a contested sector mid-siege, removing the previous visual glitch where the bar would mistakenly assume the siege had just begun.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.3[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]V3.0.3 🐛BUGFIX, ⚖️BALANCING & ⚙️ADJUSTMENTS PATCH UPDATE![/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ GAMEPLAY PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes issues regarding desyncs, memory leaks and other bugs. Balancing a few numbers, alongside a few adjustments![/i]

[b]🪲BUGFIXES[/b]
[list]
[*]🐛 [b]Event Scheduler Desync:[/b] Fixed an issue where spontaneous event timers (Fleet Clashes, Refugee Convoys, etc.) were reliant on server tick accumulation, which caused timers to stall or desync when the server lagged. Event timers now utilize persistent, absolute `Player().playtime` stamps to ensure flawless timer continuation and pacing even across server restarts and lag spikes.
[*]🐛 [b]Siege Weather Memory Leak:[/b] Fixed a critical issue where the dynamic Eclipse weather applied during Sieges was never properly cleared when the event concluded because the script's `onRemove` callback was not exposed to the engine API. Siege Weather now correctly dissipates when the event ends, preventing massive visual bloat and sector bloat.
[*]🐛 [b]Eclipse Vanguard Shield Bug:[/b] Fixed a syntax error where the Vanguard Boss was assigned a non-existent `shieldMultiplier` property instead of correctly multiplying its actual `shieldMaxDurability`, leaving it vulnerable.
[/list]

[b]🖥️BALANCING[/b]
[list]
[*]⚖️ [b]Siege Troop Transports:[/b] Troop Transport boarding timers now scale dynamically with the defending station's max durability. Instead of a flat 60 seconds to board, transports now require an additional 1 second per 100,000 HP of the station's hull (capped at 5 minutes), giving defenders realistic time windows to defend massive fortified citadels before they are annexed.
[*]⚖️ [b]Dynamic War Economy Scaling:[/b] Freelance Mercenary Payouts and High-Profile War Bounties are no longer flat rates! Both systems have been completely rebalanced to scale exponentially based on the faction's distance to the Galactic Core. Fighting for an Outer Rim faction will still yield standard rates, but shedding blood for inner-core empires will yield massive payouts scaling up to 26x the base rate.
[/list]

[b]🔧ADJUSTMENTS[/b]
[list]
[*]⚙️ [b]Living Galaxy Simulation Rates:[/b] The default CCM configuration values governing background simulations (Diplomacy, Ceasefires, Bounties, News, Trade Sanctions) have been heavily rebalanced. Previously, the simulation evaluated only 10 faction pairs every 20 minutes, which resulted in a stagnant galaxy where wars rarely broke out organically. The new default intervals have been lowered to 5-10 minutes, and the default faction pairing batch has been increased to 50.
[i]Note: These are just the new out-of-the-box defaults to provide a truly living, breathing galaxy; players can still freely adjust these timers themselves via the CCM menu![/i]
[*]⚙️ [b]Eclipse Vanguard FireRate:[/b] Reduced its FireRate multiplier from 500x down to a safer 50x to prevent massive server-side packet spam and simulation freezing.
[/list]

[i]Version 3.0.2[/i]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🐛V3.0.2 BUGFIX & OPTIMIZATION PATCH UPDATE!🛠️[/h1]
[hr][/hr]
[b]🛠️ HOTFIX PATCH[/b]
[i]This patch fixes issues regarding war contract diplomacy exploits![/i]
[*]🐛 Fixed a major exploit where players with "Excellent" standing could accept War Contracts against a faction, fly into the sector, and destroy the mission targets without retaliation.
[*]🛠️ Optimized by now accepting [i]any[/i] of the 14 War Contracts is now explicitly treated as an act of war. It will instantly plummet your reputation with the target faction by `-200,000`, forcing an immediate hostile state. A high-priority UI warning and in-game chat notification have been added to prevent players from accidentally declaring war.

